  "bodyHtml": "\n\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-168842638426899e3410/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>Michael Rudden</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2024-11-12T14:34:04-05:00\" title=\"Tuesday, November 12, 2024, 2:34 pm\">November 12, 2024</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\t<p>The Guild of Harwich Artists’ twelfth<strong> annual holiday ornament sale</strong> is a popular attraction that raises money for two local children’s charities.  This year the hand-painted ornaments will be on sale <strong>Black Friday and weekends through December 15, 11am to 4pm</strong>.  The Art Gallery will also be open late during <strong>Harwich Port Holiday Stroll on Friday, December 6</strong>.  Public parking across the street.</p>\n<p>Over 200 hand painted miniature oil canvases and framed watercolor paintings by members of the Guild are available at $20 each.</p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_7232\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img class=\"size-medium wp-image-7232\" src=\"/media/archive/1d3ddf20e30aca89c324d069554c69e2eb014532e0a3430311b5cced0298ff40.jpg\" alt=\"&quot;Gallery down the Alley&quot;\" width=\"225\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-7232\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Art Gallery Entrance</figcaption></figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_7234\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img class=\"size-medium wp-image-7234\" src=\"/media/archive/3947a93907040a7b0911f0227f31ff17503206a0f1b4cb2cef352e5c1aea56be.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"192\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" /><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-7234\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Hand Painted Holiday Ornaments</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Payment by check, cash or credit Card. Many of the ornaments are inspired by holiday images of Cape Cod and make wonderful stocking stuffers. Proceeds of this year’s ornaments sale will be split between <strong>The Children’s Center, </strong>a part of Harwich Ecumenical Council for the Homeless, and the <strong>Harwich Children’s Fund</strong>.</p>\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<footer class=\"entry-footer\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-terms category\">Posted in <a href=\"/archive/source-e23b79be08a822c7b682/\" rel=\"tag\">WHAT'S NEW</a></span>\t\t\t\t\t</footer>\n\n\t\n",
